{"agent_id":"pp3g-tm63-read-only-live-system-verification-review-do-not-6b08","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T18:58:07.469124575Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"f3d4b144-99dc-41ae-8cfb-812afd332b91","author":"pp3g-tm63-read-only-live-system-verification-review-do-not-6b08","content":"## [VERDICT] READ-ONLY breadth + adversarial review of the #125 safe re-hydration guard (fork ade6146b) WITH LIVE verification against the running ASES installation\n\nScope: the hydration gate + its callers only. Read-only: no ASES or fork files modified, no commit, no push. #125 NOT closed. All live tests reversible (fresh /tmp clone; the only live mutation — my own session-start trust commits b570eabf+6770160a — are the standard identity-registration commits, left in place).\n\n== HEADLINE ==\n\nCHANGES REQUESTED. The gate is CORRECT and WORKS for the current ASES live state (independently verified with the installed binary, trigger condition live) — but it does NOT close the family: the destructive v2 hydrate path remains reachable through (1) a live advertised command (`crosslink tui` — verified 241→4 wipe, 100% of the DB), (2) the HubMode::resolve degrade-to-V2 fail-open paths (locks/daemon/shared_writer), and (3) ANY fresh environment of the ASES remote — which is v3 but retains a pushed v2 branch — where the whole system locks into V2 mode and the ORIGINAL bug continues deterministically. The docs declaring \"RESOLVED 2026-08-06\" and the \"close-worthy for the core guard\" recommendation are premature.\n\n== PART A — LIVE VERIFICATION (installed binary at /home/claude-code/.cargo/bin/crosslink) ==\n\nA1. GATE PRESENT IN BINARY. Strings confirm strict_ref_present + \"hub is not confidently v2-only (v3 marker refs present or hub absent)\". Operational note: binary built 11:47 from a DIRTY tree (--version reports 0.9.0-beta.1+4efd9ae6-dirty — the PARENT sha); commit ade6146b made 11:53. The live-tested artifact predates the commit by ~6 min; observable behavior matches the committed tree (both contain the gate). Worth confirming the merge build reproduces before the ~50-commit push.\n\nA2. TASK (1) — LIVE HUB-TIP-ADVANCE TEST: PASSED, independently. The trigger condition arose organically: my session's key registration created trust commits b570eabf + 6770160a, advancing the v2-branch tip past the .last-hydrated-ref marker (af67d395). In this exact pre-fix-wipe state: DB stayed 241 issues before AND after multiple crosslink commands; issue list 102 lines; NO display-id collision warning; marker NOT refreshed (still af67d395) — conclusive proof the v2 path did NOT run (a v2 hydrate writes the marker AND collapses the DB to the stale projection). The gate holds for the pre-existing cache.\n\nA3. TASK (2) — REMOTE-ONLY-V3-MARKER FAIL-OPEN: CONFIRMED against the live remote, with the full mechanism chain. Evidence: (i) the ASES remote IS v3 — origin advertises refs/heads/crosslink/meta (d4d823e8) + /checkpoint (0646fb82); (ii) the remote ALSO retains refs/heads/crosslink/hub (b570eabf) — kept alive by the very writers the fix documents as out-of-scope (the trust-publish commit is PUSHED); (iii) a fresh clone + the init_v2_worktree state has meta/checkpoint ABSENT locally (only refs/remotes/origin/*) and v2 PRESENT → replaying the exact probes: meta exit=1/empty, checkpoint exit=1/empty, v2 exit=0 → hub_is_confidently_v2_only = Ok(true) → destructive v2 path RUNS. The gate probes only refs/heads/*, never refs/remotes/origin/*.\n\nA4. NEW MECHANISM (beyond hy3's probe-level reproduction) — the fresh-clone PERMANENT-V2 LOCK-IN. SyncManager::new (sync/core.rs:37-77) resolves HubMode ONCE at construction via local-only HubMode::resolve(cache_dir) (cache absent → V2). init_cache (cache.rs:166-215) takes the v2-first branch whenever has_remote_v2 (the retained remote branch) — it NEVER reaches the v3-join path (fetch_v3_refs_for_join lives only in the no-v2 else-branch) and never flips hub_mode to V3. fetch() (cache.rs:298-320) dispatches on the cached V2 → fetch_v2_readonly (fetches only the v2 branch, no marker adoption). sync_cmd → sync_v2_readonly → hydrate_to_sqlite (4 June-era files). Every subsequent command re-resolves V2 the same way. RESULT: a fresh clone of ASES today is DETERMINISTICALLY stuck in V2 mode — the v3 hub is never joined, sync always yields the 4-issue baseline, and the gate AGREES (local-only) and actively sanctions the v2 path on every marker mismatch (trust commits keep arriving from the main repo). This is the ORIGINAL bug, fully intact, in any fresh environment. hy3 reproduced the probe-level fail-open; the lock-in chain (init_cache branch precedence + cached hub_mode + fetch dispatch) is what makes it permanent and self-sustaining.\n\nA5. TASK (3) — UNGATED TUI EXPOSURE: CONFIRMED + QUANTIFIED. `crosslink tui` is a LIVE advertised command (\"Interactive terminal dashboard (read-only)\"). Two unconditional hydrate_to_sqlite call sites: tui/mod.rs:833 (startup: init_cache + fetch + hydrate_to_sqlite) and tui/mod.rs:534 (poll_sync — every 30s PERIODIC_SYNC_INTERVAL and after every manual sync; the background thread runs init_cache+fetch only, then poll_sync hydrates with NO hub-mode check and NO gate). Wipe math on a /tmp copy of the production DB: 241 issues, 241 agent-authored (created_by NOT NULL), 0 preserved, and the cache worktree IS checked out on crosslink/hub with the 4 June-era JSON files present → hydrate_to_sqlite's clear_shared_data + created_by-NULL-only preservation → 241 → 4 (100% wipe). The wipe is TIMER-DRIVEN (30s), SILENT (let _ = swallows errors), and REPEATABLE. A user running the read-only dashboard in the ASES main repo destroys the entire issue DB.\n\nA6. TASK (4) — NEW FAILURE MODES (see MUST FIX 2-3, SHOULD CONSIDER 4-7 below).\n\n== PART B — FINDINGS ==\n\nMUST FIX:\n\n1. [MUST FIX — HIGH] Ungated destructive callers outside the diff. The fix gated ONLY hydration.rs:1244 (maybe_auto_hydrate). Still-live v2-path callers:\n   - tui/mod.rs:833 + 534 — UNCONDITIONAL, hub-mode-blind. Real-world: `crosslink tui` wipes 241→4 (A5). Highest urgency: a read-only command destroys the DB.\n   - locks_cmd.rs:303 (sync_v2_readonly) — gated by hub_mode().is_v3() (line 246) which inherits the HubMode::resolve degrade-to-V2-on-error (hub_v3.rs:709-720, unchanged by the fix): a transient git failure silently re-enables the destructive path — the exact concurrent-launch race class the fix claims to address.\n   - daemon.rs:279 — same degrade-to-V2 fail-open, in a long-running process (network/transient failures most likely there).\n   - shared_writer/core.rs:220 (hydrate_with_retry) — same pattern; reached by ~20 mutation paths (mutations.rs/milestones.rs).\n   - integrity_cmd.rs:379 — v3-aware when v3_state resolves, but falls to the v2 path otherwise (operator-invoked, lower frequency).\n\n2. [MUST FIX — HIGH] Fresh-environment fail-open (A3+A4): gate + mode detection are local-ref-only. On a v3 remote that retains the v2 branch (ASES today), every fresh clone/worktree-bootstrap locks into V2 and the original wipe continues. Recommended directions (for the implementer to design): (a) init_cache joins the v3 hub when the REMOTE advertises v3 markers regardless of a retained v2 branch; and/or (b) the gate probes the remote (ls-remote refs/heads/crosslink/meta) fail-closed (unreachable remote → skip v2 path); and/or (c) delete the remote v2 branch after migration (the retained branch is the trap, kept alive by the trust-publish pushes).\n\n3. [MUST FIX — MEDIUM] Docs overstate the fix. Addendum 04 \"RESOLVED 2026-08-06\", playbook §6.5 \"durable fix\", crosslink-fork.md \"root cause fixed\", and the 12:53 result's \"recommend close-worthy for the core guard\" — while the wipe remains reachable through 3 routes (TUI, degrade-to-V2, fresh env). Systemic risk: agents will drop the compact-recovery and sequential-launch discipline exactly when the hazard persists. Annotate the RESOLVED marks with the residual scope or hold them until the caller coverage is closed.\n\nSHOULD CONSIDER:\n\n4. Test (b) passes by construction — non-discriminating. The v2-only fixture (setup_git_env_with_v2_cache) yields the same outcome with the gate removed (hydrate runs, issue 7 imported, assert passes). The 11:54 result's claim \"all 3 FAIL with the gate removed\" is FALSE for test (b). (Reading-proven; corroborates hy3's mutation matrix.)\n\n5. Test (c) does not exercise strict_ref_present's discriminator. The fixture creates BOTH markers then corrupts only meta — checkpoint remains VALID, so strict (Err→skip) and pre-fix lenient (meta collapsed absent, checkpoint present→skip) give the SAME outcome. The novel primitive has zero regression coverage. The discriminating fixture (broken meta + checkpoint ABSENT + v2 present: strict skips, lenient RUNS) must be added — hy3 wrote and verified it; it should be committed.\n\n6. Gate-probe TOCTOU race (fresh-env only, small window): probe-then-act without a lock — a concurrent process creating local markers (bootstrap/join/fetch) between the probe and hydrate_to_sqlite executes a stale decision. Same class as the #123/#124/#137 concurrent-launch race; the fix does not serialize hydration.\n\n7. Marker never refreshed on the gate-skip path: on a v3 hub the marker tracks the V2-branch tip (hub_head_ref = cache worktree HEAD), so every trust/agent/swarm tip move re-triggers the 3-subprocess probe until the next explicit sync. Writing current_ref on the skip path would bound the probe to actual moves. Minor perf; note the probe is otherwise well-behaved (git spawn failure → Err → skip, verified).\n\nNITS:\n8. TUI hydration errors are swallowed (`let _ =`), hiding even partial failures.\n9. The #427 empty-dir guard is defeated by any single stale file (the 4 June-era files) — pre-existing, reinforced.\n10. Old-style v3 refs (refs/crosslink/{meta,checkpoint} without /heads/) are not probed — consistent with classify_hub_version (no NEW divergence), but a v3 layout the gate would treat as v2-only.\n\n== PART C — WHAT PASSED / HONESTY ==\n\nPassed and independently verified: (1) the gate's strict_ref_present semantics (empirical git 2.x behavior: clean-missing=exit1/empty → absent; broken loose ref=exit1+stderr → Err→skip; non-repo=exit128 → Err→skip); (2) the gate placement after the marker check (hot path unchanged); (3) the reading-(a) semantics for the ASES live state (skip, no double-hydration; sync_cmd/daemon/shared_writer v3 paths unchanged and working — my sync hydrated 237 issues via v3); (4) the fix's claim \"hub_is_confidently_v2_only returns Ok(false) when v3 marker refs present\" — TRUE for the current local state; (5) the writer comments in agent.rs/trust.rs/lifecycle.rs are comment-only (no behavior change). Findings 1-2 of hy3 (ungated callers, HubMode fail-open, remote-only fail-open) and the test-quality findings (b/c) are independently confirmed with additional live evidence; the new contributions are A4 (permanent-V2 lock-in), A5 (quantified timer-driven TUI wipe), A2 (independent live pass), and findings 3/6/7 (docs overstatement, TOCTOU, marker-never-refreshed).\n\n== BOTTOM LINE ==\n\nThe gate is a correct and necessary first layer and it DOES protect the current ASES main repo (verified live). It is NOT the durable family fix the docs claim: the destructive v2 path remains reachable via a live read-only command (TUI — 100% wipe), via degrade-to-V2 under transient git failure (locks/daemon/shared_writer), and via every fresh environment of the v3 remote (permanent V2 lock-in, original bug intact). Close the caller coverage (at minimum gate the TUI paths and add remote-probing to mode detection), add the discriminating test (c) fixture and a test-(b) discriminator, and correct the RESOLVED documentation before this is merged/pushed as the durable fix. #125 stays OPEN.","created_at":"2026-08-06T18:58:07.462734344Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:bVMAMz5ZBBRHfg28oPzrfgzgLf9XGnOHABIY15Om2ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUuwpG2CErbCpDC0fZMn/h/yuzb7AUOhA4hfyrRl4gZMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA5SsyqGCdXlCfGJwEx5dTerhYMQhYeAdpbQbzRP1A4vHoWnLSM4/gWN/iZB6q3DJq1n7FJG8I611HG51ve8R6BA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:bVMAMz5ZBBRHfg28oPzrfgzgLf9XGnOHABIY15Om2ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUuwpG2CErbCpDC0fZMn/h/yuzb7AUOhA4hfyrRl4gZMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFKWwQp35D/pnFjvi4wNrdkHZMHq5o8Gu4FOSixeuJrpKHQ+j6mYnz2vh2bTUfTD+ckpDv7mzg5Kh2EL2X0ZuAI="}
